<!--
    Amharic, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    The driver is addressed in the polite form (እርስዎ), which is also the same for men and women.
    "Vehicle" is መኪና, the everyday word drivers use for any vehicle (ተሽከርካሪ is the formal one);
    "run" is ዙር; "trip" is ጉዞ; "report" is ሪፖርት; "dispatcher" is ተቆጣጣሪ; "block" is ብሎክ;
    "route" is መስመር; "stop" is ፌርማታ; "agency" is ድርጅት; "driver" is ሹፌር; "app" is መተግበሪያ;
    "location" is አካባቢ, as Android's Amharic settings say; "diagnostics" is የመተግበሪያ መረጃ.
    Spelling follows the simplified forms phones use (ስራ, ሶስት, መሰረት). Distances keep m and km.
-->
